WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Hang a 20 newton load
on a thin steel wire.

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.680
It stretches.

3
00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.560
Hang the same load on a thick steel cable.

4
00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:09.170
It stretches less.

5
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.210
Same steel.

6
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.380
Same load.

7
00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.840
Different stretch.

8
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:17.020
So why does the thin wire stretch
more than the thick cable?

9
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.000
In this mission, you'll meet a number
that belongs to the steel itself,

10
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.170
not to the wire or the cable.

11
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.490
Then you'll stretch a long,
thin wire over a pulley,

12
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.120
add load in steps, and measure
that number for yourself.

13
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:35.240
Your mission: explain why the thin wire
stretches more under the same load.
